<SiteLayout title="Conditions We Support | Otter Homecare" description="Compassionate, specialist home care for dementia, stroke recovery, palliative needs and physical disabilities across Wiltshire and Somerset. Personalised, dignified care at home.">
<header class="phero"> <div class="wrap"> <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> · <a href="/care-services">Care Services</a> · Conditions</div> <h1>Conditions we support</h1> <p>Caring for a range of conditions with compassion and expertise — always with kindness, respect and the highest standards of care, in the comfort of your own home.</p> </div> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="wrap"> <div class="reveal" style="max-width:62ch"> <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:14px">We support people living with a variety of conditions — from dementia and stroke recovery to those living with physical disabilities or nearing end of life. Our approach is always personalised, enabling our clients to stay in the comfort of their own home while receiving tailored, dignified care.</p> <p class="lede">Every person's situation is unique. That's why we take time to get to know you and your family — so we can match the right Care Professionals and plan support that truly fits.</p> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section trustwhy" style="padding-top:0"> <div class="wrap"> <div class="trust3" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)"><div class="t3 reveal"><img src="/img/cond-dementia.jpg" alt="Caring support for someone living with dementia" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover;border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:18px;display:block;box-shadow:0 10px 26px -16px rgba(15,79,96,.5)"><span class="ix">01</span><h3>Dementia</h3><p>Specialist, person-centred dementia care with a small, familiar team and training co-produced with Alzheimer's Support. <a href="/dementia" style="color:var(--clay-text);font-weight:700;white-space:nowrap">See our dementia care →</a></p></div><div class="t3 reveal"><img src="/img/cond-stroke.jpg" alt="Supporting recovery after a stroke" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover;border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:18px;display:block;box-shadow:0 10px 26px -16px rgba(15,79,96,.5)"><span class="ix">02</span><h3>Stroke recovery</h3><p>Practical, patient support after a stroke — help with mobility, personal care, meals, medication and confidence, rebuilding routine at home at the right pace, alongside any therapy team.</p></div><div class="t3 reveal"><img src="/img/personal-care-real.jpg" alt="Patient, adaptable support day to day" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover;border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:18px;display:block;box-shadow:0 10px 26px -16px rgba(15,79,96,.5)"><span class="ix">03</span><h3>Parkinson's</h3><p>Care that adapts to changing days — support with movement, medication timing, meals and the everyday tasks that get harder, always with patience and dignity.</p></div><div class="t3 reveal"><img src="/img/cond-eol.jpg" alt="Gentle end-of-life care" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover;border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:18px;display:block;box-shadow:0 10px 26px -16px rgba(15,79,96,.5)"><span class="ix">04</span><h3>Palliative &amp; End-of-Life</h3><p>Gentle, dignified support to stay comfortable at home, working closely with district nurses and the family, so precious time is spent the way it should be.</p></div><div class="t3 reveal"><img src="/img/cond-disabilities.jpg" alt="Support to live well with a physical disability" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover;border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:18px;display:block;box-shadow:0 10px 26px -16px rgba(15,79,96,.5)"><span class="ix">05</span><h3>Physical Disabilities</h3><p>Enabling, respectful support that puts independence first — help where it's wanted, never taking over, built around how you like things done.</p></div><div class="t3 reveal"><img src="/img/out-and-about.jpg" alt="Rebuilding confidence after a fall" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover;border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:18px;display:block;box-shadow:0 10px 26px -16px rgba(15,79,96,.5)"><span class="ix">06</span><h3>Fall Recovery</h3><p>Confidence and strength after a fall — practical, reassuring help to get moving safely again at home. <a href="/fall-recovery" style="color:var(--clay-text);font-weight:700;white-space:nowrap">See our fall recovery support →</a></p></div></div>
      <p class="lede reveal" style="text-align:center;max-width:60ch;margin:40px auto 0">Our Care Professionals are trained to care for a variety of conditions. If your loved one has a condition not listed here, or you're unsure what support they might need, we're always happy to offer advice.</p> </div> </section> <section class="section book" id="book-cta"> <div class="wrap" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;text-align:center;display:block"> <div class="reveal" style="max-width:36ch;margin:0 auto"> <span class="eyebrow" style="color:#9fc4bf">Free, no-obligation assessment</span> <h2 style="margin:14px 0 12px">Let's find the right care, together</h2> <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:26px;color:#bfe0dc">Speak to a real, local person who can talk you through the support available.</p> <div style="display:flex;gap:13px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap"> <a class="btn btn-clay btn-lg" href="/contact">Book a free assessment</a> <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="tel:01225690022" style="background:transparent;color:#fff;border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5)">Call 01225 690022</a> </div> </div> </div> </section>
</SiteLayout>
